cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use CableDyn in academic work, please cite the journal article given
  as the preferred citation. To identify the exact software release used, also
  cite this software entry with its version.
title: "CableDyn: A cable and mooring dynamics solver for floating offshore wind"
type: software
abstract: >-
  CableDyn is an open-source finite-element solver for the static and dynamic
  analysis of offshore mooring lines and dynamic power cables. It combines
  tension-only elements for moorings with cubic-Hermite finite-bending elements
  for power cables, solves the static equilibrium by Newton's method, and
  integrates the dynamics with the implicit generalised-alpha scheme. It runs as
  a standalone program, as an OpenFAST mooring module, through a C interface, or
  from Python.
